# Gate step 1968-2wpe — the forge installs the agy CLI once, onto the
# persistent tool-cache volume, and a warm launch neither downloads it nor
# runs `agy update` inside the refresh window. Measured on yoga 2026-11-02:
# every warm launch re-downloaded agy (5.7 / 6.2 s) because it was installed
# into the --rm container's /usr/local/bin. The arms execute the real
# require_antigravity cut out of images/default/lib-common.sh with stub curl
# and agy; no network, no podman.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking a warm forge launch reuses its cached agy CLI (1968-2wpe)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-agy-install-cached.lua"
